Replace YOUR_SERVER_IP with the actual IP, e.g. http://185.22.44.211.

Since you do not have a domain yet, ALLOWED_HOSTS=* is acceptable for the initial setup


cd /opt/preciselab
docker compose up -d --build

docker compose ps
docker compose logs -f web

if needed:
docker compose exec web python manage.py migrate --noinput
docker compose exec web python manage.py collectstatic --noinput
docker compose exec web python manage.py check



install nginx:
sudo apt-get install -y nginx
create config:
sudo nano /etc/nginx/sites-available/preciselab

use:

server {
    listen 80;
    server_name _;
    location / {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    }
}

enable it: 

sudo ln -sf /etc/nginx/sites-available/preciselab /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/preciselab
sudo rm -f /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/default
sudo nginx -t
sudo systemctl reload nginx

Now the app should be reachable at:
http://YOUR_SERVER_IP


If you want HTTPS on an IP, you can use a self-signed certificate:
sudo apt-get install -y openssl
mkdir -p /etc/ssl/preciselab
openssl req -x509 -nodes -newkey rsa:2048 \
  -keyout /etc/ssl/preciselab/key.pem \
  -out /etc/ssl/preciselab/cert.pem \
  -days 365 \
  -subj "/CN=YOUR_SERVER_IP"

Then configure Nginx with SSL:

server {
    listen 80;
    server_name _;
    return 301 https://$host$request_uri;
}

server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    server_name _;

    ssl_certificate /etc/ssl/preciselab/cert.pem;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/ssl/preciselab/key.pem;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    }
}


Then reload Nginx:
sudo nginx -t
sudo systemctl reload nginx

open:
https://YOUR_SERVER_IP



Best path for now
Use this configuration order:

IP-only server → Nginx on 80/443
self-signed cert if no domain yet
add real domain later and swap the cert and ALLOWED_HOSTS
If you want, I can give you:

a copy-paste install-docker.sh script, or
a ready-to-use Nginx config for IP-only deployment.






